# CI/CD Conventions

## Action Versions

Pin to specific version tags (not `@master` or `@latest`):

```yaml
# GOOD — pinned versions
uses: actions/checkout@v4
uses: actions/setup-go@v5
uses: golangci/golangci-lint-action@v7
uses: goreleaser/goreleaser-action@v6
uses: codecov/codecov-action@v5
uses: securego/gosec@v2.23.0

# BAD — breaks without warning
uses: securego/gosec@master
uses: securego/gosec@v2  # tag doesn't exist
```

## Go Version Strategy

- `go.mod`: Set to the minimum supported version (currently `1.24`)
- CI test matrix: Test the two most recent Go releases
- Release workflow: Use `>=1.24` to get latest stable

## Linting

- golangci-lint uses v2 config format (`.golangci.yml` with `version: "2"`)
- Pin `golangci-lint-action@v6` to an explicit v2 version (e.g., `version: v2.9.0`), since `latest` resolves to v1

## Releases

- GoReleaser v2 config in `.goreleaser.yml`
- Version injected via ldflags: `-X github.com/coredds/enigoma.Version={{.Version}}`
- Triggered by `v*` tags on push
